            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of diet on the biochemical parameters of blood in the population of the Asian North].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The studies have shown that the diet of the native residents of Taimyr is imbalanced of the major nutrients (high uptake of carbohydrates and low uptake of fats and proteins). A certain correlation has been found between the higher incidence rates of coronary heart disease, blood atherogenic lipoprotein levels and changed diet pattern.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
